      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum single dose of about 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily with meals\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into divided doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. I'd recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
